# `as BASENS` binds the Namespace OBJECT, which is what this setUp needs:
# `self.basens` is read by the other methods of the TestCase, long after the
# block ends (record ldpy/027). The prefix is declared at module level so the
# other methods can also write `basens:term`, which is the whole point of
# having it lexical as well.
@prefix basens: <http://example.org/base/> as BASENS .

def setUp(self):
